What happens if an application connects to a different node in RAC Architecture?
In Oracle RAC, if an application connects to a different node, data consistency is maintained using Global Cache Service (GCS) and Cache Fusion, which transfer data between nodes if needed. Load balancing ensures efficient request distribution, and if a node fails, VIP failover, Transparent Application Failover (TAF), or Fast Connection Failover (FCF) seamlessly reconnects the application to another node, ensuring high availability.

